<% content_for :title, "Privacy" %>
<% content_for :head do %>
  <meta name="description" content="What beckit stores, who can see it, and how to export or delete it.">
<% end %>

<%# Plain-language summary of what the code does today. Update it whenever storage, cookies or third parties change. %>
<% section_heading = "font-display text-2xl font-medium tracking-tight text-stone-900 dark:text-white" %>
<% body = "flex flex-col gap-4 text-base/7 text-pretty text-stone-700 dark:text-stone-300 [&_li]:pl-1 [&_ul]:list-disc [&_ul]:pl-5" %>
<div class="page">
  <article class="flex max-w-[68ch] flex-col gap-12">
    <div>
      <h1 class="font-display text-4xl font-medium tracking-tight text-balance text-stone-900 dark:text-white">Privacy</h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-lg/8 text-pretty text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-400">beckit is a private journal. This page explains, in plain terms, what it keeps and what you can do about it.</p>
    </div>

    <section aria-labelledby="stores_heading" class="flex flex-col gap-4">
      <h2 id="stores_heading" class="<%= section_heading %>">What beckit stores</h2>
      <div class="<%= body %>">
        <ul role="list">
          <li>Your name, email address and password. The password is stored as a one-way hash, never as the password itself.</li>
          <li>Anything you add in Settings: a preferred name, date of birth, photo, time zone and crisis contact. All of these are optional except the time zone.</li>
          <li>Your journal entries and the thinking traps you tag them with.</li>
          <li>For each sign-in: the IP address and browser it came from, so a session can be recognized and ended.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>While you write an entry, unsaved text is kept in your browser tab so a reload doesn't lose it. It is removed when you save, cancel or close the tab.</p>
        <p>When you delete an entry it is hidden straight away, so a mistake can be undone, and permanently removed after <%= Situation::RESTORE_WINDOW.inspect %>.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="sees_heading" class="flex flex-col gap-4">
      <h2 id="sees_heading" class="<%= section_heading %>">Who can see it</h2>
      <div class="<%= body %>">
        <p>Only you, when signed in. beckit has no screen for anyone else to read your entries, and it doesn't share, sell or analyze them for advertising.</p>
        <p>Like any hosted service, the people who run the server could reach the database directly.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="cookies_heading" class="flex flex-col gap-4">
      <h2 id="cookies_heading" class="<%= section_heading %>">Cookies and outside services</h2>
      <div class="<%= body %>">
        <p>beckit sets one cookie to keep you signed in. If you leave "Keep me signed in" unchecked, it ends when you close your browser. There are no advertising or analytics cookies.</p>
        <p>Pages load fonts and images from beckit itself, not from outside services, so other companies aren't told when you visit.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="controls_heading" class="flex flex-col gap-4">
      <h2 id="controls_heading" class="<%= section_heading %>">Your controls</h2>
      <div class="<%= body %>">
        <p>In <%= link_to "Settings", edit_settings_path, class: "font-medium text-teal-700 underline decoration-teal-700/30 underline-offset-2 hover:decoration-teal-700 dark:text-teal-400 dark:decoration-teal-400/30" %>, under Account, you can:</p>
        <ul role="list">
          <li>Download all of your entries as a CSV file.</li>
          <li>Change your password, which signs out your other devices.</li>
          <li>Delete your account. This removes your account, every entry (including recently deleted ones), photo and sign-ins from the app straight away.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
</div>
